SpiderMonkey on Haiku arm64: wasm trap context, JIT icache flush, libbe for DateTime

On top of HaikuPorts' firefox-157.0.1.patchset (x86_64 only):
- WasmSignalHandlers.cpp: the XP_HAIKU block defines only x86 registers. On arm64,
  mcontext_t is struct vregs (headers/posix/arch/arm64/signal.h): pc = elr, fp = x[29],
  lr, sp; the kernel restores all four on sigreturn (arch_restore_signal_frame), so the
  wasm trap handler can redirect the pc.
- MozCpu-vixl.cpp: EnsureIAndDCacheCoherency #errors for OSes other than Linux/Android/
  FreeBSD. Haiku allows EL0 cache maintenance and CTR_EL0 reads (the EFI loader sets
  SCTLR_EL1.UCI and UCT), so the user-mode dc civac / ic ivau sequence applies as is.
- vm/moz.build: the patchset's DateTime.cpp asks BLocaleRoster for the time zone; the
  standalone shell must then link libbe (libxul gets it from toolkit/library).
- rust/moz.build: jsrust carries the Rust standard library, which needs libbsd
  (arc4random_buf; toolkit/library/rust does the same for gkrust) and libnetwork (sockets).

diff --git a/js/src/jit/arm64/vixl/MozCpu-vixl.cpp b/js/src/jit/arm64/vixl/MozCpu-vixl.cpp
index 2839823785..c315bfeecb 100644
--- a/js/src/jit/arm64/vixl/MozCpu-vixl.cpp
+++ b/js/src/jit/arm64/vixl/MozCpu-vixl.cpp
@@ -115,7 +115,7 @@ void CPU::EnsureIAndDCacheCoherency(void* address, size_t length) {
   FlushInstructionCache(GetCurrentProcess(), address, length);
 #elif defined(XP_DARWIN)
   sys_icache_invalidate(address, length);
-#elif defined(__aarch64__) && (defined(__linux__) || defined(__android__) || defined(__FreeBSD__))
+#elif defined(__aarch64__) && (defined(__linux__) || defined(__android__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__HAIKU__))
   // Implement the cache synchronisation for all targets where AArch64 is the
   // host, even if we're building the simulator for an AAarch64 host. This
   // allows for cases where the user wants to simulate code as well as run it
@@ -125,7 +125,8 @@ void CPU::EnsureIAndDCacheCoherency(void* address, size_t length) {
     return;
   }
 
-  // The code below assumes user space cache operations are allowed.
+  // The code below assumes user space cache operations are allowed (on Haiku,
+  // the kernel sets SCTLR_EL1.UCI and UCT).
 
   // Work out the line sizes for each cache, and use them to determine the
   // start addresses.
diff --git a/js/src/rust/moz.build b/js/src/rust/moz.build
index 6d73d29e19..8fe5975720 100644
--- a/js/src/rust/moz.build
+++ b/js/src/rust/moz.build
@@ -25,6 +25,13 @@ if CONFIG["OS_ARCH"] == "Darwin":
     # The Rust standard library references libresolv on macOS, so we need to
     # link it as a workaround. See also bug 1367932.
     OS_LIBS += ["-lresolv"]
+elif CONFIG["OS_ARCH"] == "Haiku":
+    # The Rust standard library uses arc4random_buf() (libbsd) and the socket
+    # functions (libnetwork).
+    OS_LIBS += [
+        "bsd",
+        "network",
+    ]
 elif CONFIG["OS_ARCH"] == "WINNT":
     # Extra libraries used by Rust bindings libs in debug builds.
     OS_LIBS += [
diff --git a/js/src/vm/moz.build b/js/src/vm/moz.build
index b0646c7575..a862cd1c7f 100644
--- a/js/src/vm/moz.build
+++ b/js/src/vm/moz.build
@@ -155,3 +155,7 @@ if CONFIG["USE_LIBZ_RS"]:
 
 if CONFIG["FUZZING_JS_FUZZILLI"]:
     include("/tools/fuzzing/libfuzzer-config.mozbuild")
